{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E6jRiLnTQfjs75RYA1v4Mc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tset: Quillbrook Village Hall\n3\trole: governing\n4\tcovers: \"Trustee membership, voting, meetings and decision-making authority\"\n5\t---\n6\t# Trustee Committee Rules\n7\tQuillbrook Village Hall is a fictional organisation.\n8\t\n9\t## 1. Purpose\n10\t1.1 The committee manages the hall for community use.\n11\t1.2 It may hire out rooms and equipment under hall-bookings.md.\n12\t1.3 These rules were adopted on 12 February 2025.\n13\t\n14\t## 2. Committee membership\n15\t2.1 The committee has between five and nine trustees.\n16\t2.2 Trustees must be at least 18 years old.\n17\t2.3 Applicants must live in Quillbrook or a neighbouring village.\n18\t2.4 A trustee serves for two years and may stand again.\n19\t2.5 Trustees receive no payment for committee work.\n20\t\n21\t## 3. Appointment and departure\n22\t3.1 New trustees are elected at the annual public meeting.\n23\t3.2 Election requires more than half of votes cast.\n24\t3.3 The committee may fill vacancies until the next annual meeting.\n25\t3.4 A trustee may resign by giving written notice.\n26\t3.5 Three consecutive missed meetings without explanation trigger a review.\n27\t\n28\t## 4. Meetings and votes\n29\t4.1 The committee meets at least six times each calendar year.\n30\t4.2 Four trustees form a quorum.\n31\t4.3 Decisions require a majority of those present and voting.\n32\t4.4 The chair has a casting vote if votes are equal.\n33\t4.5 Minutes must be approved at the next meeting.\n34\t\n35\t## 5. Spending authority\n36\t5.1 The treasurer may approve routine spending up to £150.\n37\t5.2 Spending above £150 requires a committee vote.\n38\t5.3 Emergency safety spending follows hall-safety.md section 5.\n39\t5.4 Two trustees must approve payments above £500.\n40\t\n41\t## 6. Matters not covered\n42\t6.1 These rules do not set a maximum number of trustee terms.\n43\t6.2 They do not prescribe a method for resolving personal disputes.\n44\t6.3 They do not specify whether trustees may attend remotely.\n45\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d262b10-5fb3-482e-b96c-c8a52ddb1b12","uuid":"836143cf-922b-4d1b-be4f-89a500941e5b","timestamp":"2026-10-13T00:23:03.794Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\tc\\open-JP2Q\\w2\\reference\\hall\\hall-trustees.md","content":"---\nset: Quillbrook Village Hall\nrole: governing\ncovers: \"Trustee membership, voting, meetings and decision-making authority\"\n---\n# Trustee Committee Rules\nQuillbrook Village Hall is a fictional organisation.\n\n## 1. Purpose\n1.1 The committee manages the hall for community use.\n1.2 It may hire out rooms and equipment under hall-bookings.md.\n1.3 These rules were adopted on 12 February 2025.\n\n## 2. Committee membership\n2.1 The committee has between five and nine trustees.\n2.2 Trustees must be at least 18 years old.\n2.3 Applicants must live in Quillbrook or a neighbouring village.\n2.4 A trustee serves for two years and may stand again.\n2.5 Trustees receive no payment for committee work.\n\n## 3. Appointment and departure\n3.1 New trustees are elected at the annual public meeting.\n3.2 Election requires more than half of votes cast.\n3.3 The committee may fill vacancies until the next annual meeting.\n3.4 A trustee may resign by giving written notice.\n3.5 Three consecutive missed meetings without explanation trigger a review.\n\n## 4. Meetings and votes\n4.1 The committee meets at least six times each calendar year.\n4.2 Four trustees form a quorum.\n4.3 Decisions require a majority of those present and voting.\n4.4 The chair has a casting vote if votes are equal.\n4.5 Minutes must be approved at the next meeting.\n\n## 5. Spending authority\n5.1 The treasurer may approve routine spending up to £150.\n5.2 Spending above £150 requires a committee vote.\n5.3 Emergency safety spending follows hall-safety.md section 5.\n5.4 Two trustees must approve payments above £500.\n\n## 6. Matters not covered\n6.1 These rules do not set a maximum number of trustee terms.\n6.2 They do not prescribe a method for resolving personal disputes.\n6.3 They do not specify whether trustees may attend remotely.\n","numLines":45,"startLine":1,"totalLines":45}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01E6jRiLnTQfjs75RYA1v4Mc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
